        "original_id": "c57f4453-c6a0-5c2f-93dc-65c6a46feaa0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kendrick Lamar, DJ Dahi, Drake, Jay Rock, Big Sean, Ariana Grande, Dacoury Natchel, Michael Carlson, Leland Wayne\n- Works: “Money Trees”, Good Kid, M.A.A.D City, Section.80, “Worst Behavior”, “Research”\n- Roles: American hip hop recording artist, rapper, producer\n\nFacts:\n- In 2011, Kendrick Lamar released his debut studio album Section.80 independently and exclusively through the iTunes Store.\n- In 2012, Kendrick Lamar released Good Kid, M.A.A.D City as his second studio album.\n- “Money Trees” is a song by Kendrick Lamar from his major label debut studio album Good Kid, M.A.A.D City.\n- DJ Dahi produced Kendrick Lamar’s song “Money Trees,” which features Jay Rock.\n- DJ Dahi is also known for producing Drake’s song “Worst Behavior.”\n- The song “Research” was written by Big Sean, Ariana Grande, Dacoury Natchel, Michael Carlson, and Leland Wayne, and it was produced by DJ Dahi and Metro Boomin.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
